    <entry_item>
      <dico>Lessing</dico>
      <unicode>ᠭᠡᠮᠲᠥᠺᠥ</unicode>
      <uighur>gemtükü</uighur>
      <cyrillic>гэмтэх</cyrillic>
      <transcript>GEMTY-</transcript>
      <definition>[=gemte-] v. i , To be[come] injured or damaged; to be[come] guilty; to commit ( a fault or crime; to fall ill; to be spoiled, injured, impaired.</definition>
      <page>376</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠭᠡᠮᠲᠥᠭᠰᠡᠨ</unicode>
          <transcript>--gsen</transcript>
          <definition> Defective, hurt, injured.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠭᠡᠮᠲᠥᠭᠰᠡᠨ ᠦᠭᠡᠢ</unicode>
          <transcript>--gsen ygei</transcript>
          <definition> Unhurt, uninjured.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠶᠠᠰᠤ ᠭᠡᠮᠲᠥᠺᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>jasu --ky </transcript>
          <definition>For a bone or bones to become injured</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠺᠥᠯ ᠭᠡᠮᠲᠥᠵᠦᠺᠦᠢ</unicode>
          <transcript>køl --zykyi </transcript>
          <definition> The foot is injured.</definition>
        </example>
      </examples>
    </entry_item>
    <entry_item>
      <dico>Chinese</dico>
      <unicode>ᠭᠡᠮᠲᠦᠬᠦ</unicode>
      <cyrillic>гэмтэх</cyrillic>
      <definition>〔动〕损坏，发生毛病，出纰漏，犯过失，出弊病；受伤；败坏，衰萎：~ эвдрэх 损坏；яс ~ 骨头损坏；骨碎；ногоо ~ 草衰萎；гэмтсэн бараа 损伤的货物；гэмтснээс цус гоожих 外伤性出血；гэмтсэн шугам 折线.</definition>
      <page>350</page>
    </entry_item>
    <entry_item>
